{% extends 'support/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block support_title %}Users &amp; Bulk Roster Import Guide{% endblock %}

{% block support_content %}
<h2 class="fs-2xl fw-800 text-white mb-2">Users &amp; Bulk Roster Import Guide</h2>
<p class="fs-md text-secondary mb-6 lh-relaxed">
    Learn how to manage your employee directory, upload records in bulk using the CSV Import Wizard, configure manager permissions, and handle security lockouts.
</p>

<!-- ── Video Section 2: Import Records ── -->
<div class="mb-8 p-6 glass-panel" style="border-radius: var(--radius-md); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12); background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25);">
    <h3 class="fs-xl fw-700 text-white mb-3 d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
        <span class="material-icons text-primary fs-xl">play_circle_filled</span>
        Video Tutorial: Importing Student &amp; User Records
    </h3>
    <p class="fs-sm text-secondary mb-5 lh-relaxed">
        Watch this video tutorial showing how to upload a CSV spreadsheet, map columns, resolve duplicate records, and generate employee check-in PINs.
    </p>

    <div class="video-embed-wrapper mb-4" style="position: relative; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; min-height: 380px; border-radius: var(--radius-md); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12); box-shadow: var(--shadow-md); background: #000; overflow: hidden;">
        <iframe 
            src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/bSwzQSQ-XuY?rel=0" 
            title="Import Records Tutorial" 
            allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" 
            allowfullscreen
            style="width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; display: block;">
        </iframe>
    </div>
</div>

<h3 class="fs-lg fw-700 text-white mb-3">1. CSV Import Wizard Step-by-Step</h3>
<p class="fs-sm text-secondary mb-4 lh-relaxed">
    Instead of adding users individually, the CSV Import Wizard lets you upload large roster lists seamlessly:
</p>

<ol class="fs-sm text-secondary d-flex flex-column gap-4 pl-5 lh-relaxed mb-8">
    <li>
        <strong>Upload CSV File:</strong> Go to <em>Users &gt; Import CSV</em> in your manager console. Select any standard `.csv` spreadsheet file containing employee or student details.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Flexible Column Mapping:</strong> The wizard automatically parses your CSV headers. Map your spreadsheet's columns (e.g. `First Name`, `Last Name`, `Phone`, `Email`, `Unique Student ID`) to CenterTime's target fields. You do not need to rename your original CSV columns prior to uploading.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Intelligent Duplicate &amp; Conflict Matching:</strong> The import engine runs multi-stage matching logic to detect existing users:
        <ul class="mt-2 d-flex flex-column gap-1 pl-4">
            <li><em>Unique ID Match:</em> Matches exact student IDs or employee numbers.</li>
            <li><em>Compound Match:</em> Matches First Name + Last Name combined with Email or Phone Number.</li>
            <li><em>Conflict Resolution:</em> For detected duplicates, choose whether to <strong>Update Existing Record</strong>, <strong>Skip Duplicate</strong>, or <strong>Force Add as New User</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Automatic PIN Generation &amp; Status Assignment:</strong> New imported users are automatically allocated a unique 4-digit check-in PIN (e.g., `A102`). If your CSV includes pre-existing PINs or unique IDs, they are preserved.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Subscription Plan Capacity Validation:</strong> The wizard verifies your imported user count against your active plan's user quota (e.g. 15 for Basic, 50 for Silver, 250 for Gold). Any records exceeding your active quota are marked as pending until plan upgrading.
    </li>
</ol>

<hr class="my-6" style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08)">

<div class="support-split-view mb-8">
    <div>
        <h3 class="fs-lg fw-700 text-white mb-3">2. Employee Roster Management</h3>
        <p class="fs-sm text-secondary mb-4 lh-relaxed">
            The User Management screen provides full oversight of your employee list:
        </p>
        <ul class="fs-sm text-secondary d-flex flex-column gap-2 pl-5 lh-relaxed mb-4">
            <li><strong>Quick Search &amp; Filter:</strong> Instantly filter by name, phone number, email address, or unique ID.</li>
            <li><strong>Active / Inactive Toggle:</strong> Deactivate staff members who leave without deleting their historical attendance data.</li>
            <li><strong>PIN Reset &amp; Management:</strong> Managers can generate a new random PIN or set a specific 4-digit PIN for any user.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-panel p-2 d-flex flex-column align-items-center" style="border-radius: var(--radius-sm); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); background: rgba(0,0,0,0.2);">
        <img src="{{ asset('img/support/users.png') }}" alt="Users List View" style="width: 100%; border-radius: var(--radius-xs); height: auto; box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);">
        <span class="fs-xs text-muted mt-2 text-center">Roster Management View</span>
    </div>
</div>

<hr class="my-6" style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08)">

<h3 class="fs-lg fw-700 text-white mb-3">3. Manager Roles &amp; Security Lockouts</h3>
<div class="d-flex flex-column gap-4 mb-6">
    <div class="p-4 rounded-sm bg-input border" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--primary) !important;">
        <h4 class="fs-md fw-600 text-white mb-1">Full Administrator vs Supervisor</h4>
        <p class="fs-sm text-secondary m-0 lh-relaxed">
            Full Administrators can manage settings, billing, categories, and managers. Supervisors can view dashboards, look up user lists, force clock-out active users, and download reports without access to core billing or settings.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-sm bg-input border" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--danger) !important;">
        <h4 class="fs-md fw-600 text-white mb-1">Unlocking PIN Lockouts</h4>
        <p class="fs-sm text-secondary m-0 lh-relaxed">
            If an employee enters an invalid PIN three consecutive times, their account displays a red <strong>Blocked (PIN Lockout)</strong> status to prevent unauthorized access. Managers can click <em>Unlock Account</em> in the user options menu to restore access.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
